  "id": "general-transfer",
  "term": "general transfer",
  "definition": "General transfer is the carryover of a broadly trained underlying process, such as attention, memory, thinking, or visual perception, into a more specific performance setting. In this source, it refers to limited transfer of these isolated processes, without strong adaptation to the real behavioral and contextual demands of the task.",
